At this juncture, it is relevant to point out the duties of an Investigator which is highlighted in the book ?Encyclopedia ? Police Law and Crimes (Vinod Publications) Vol.I, Edition 2015?
1) Ask himself the basic questions who, what, where, when, why, and how;
2) Evaluate the crime scene and determine if, in fact, a crime has occurred;
3) Locate and interview all possible witnesses;
4) Collect and preserve any and all pertinent evidence;
5) Obtain information who committed the crime through various sources, including informants;
6) Locate, question, and arrest suspect(s);
7) Organize all facts and information and build a sound case;
8) Complete the final report and resent it to the prosecutor for trial;
9) Act, when necessary, as the key witness during the trial; e.g., in a case with no eyewitnesses and the case is built on the information and evidence compiled by the investigator.?
